<title>CHINA: SHANGRI-LA AIMS FOR CWTC SPINOFF IN 1997.</title>
<headline>SHANGRI-LA AIMS FOR CWTC SPINOFF IN 1997.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The H-share flotation for Shangri-La Asia Ltd's unit China World Trade Center (CWTC) is still planned for 1997, managing director Paul Bush said.</p>
<p>China World Trade Center is a Sino-foreign joint venture owned 50 percent by Shangri-La Asia.</p>
<p>&quot;There are ongoing discussions to establish the structure of the listing and the timing. It is still projected to occur this year,&quot; Bush told a news conference on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Bush said the deal was taking time to structure because there were a number of unique features involved in this first H-share listing of a Sino-foreign joint venture.</p>
<p>H-shares are shares of China-incorporated companies listed on the Hong Kong stock market. -- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
